input: {
    "context": "{\"citation\": \"S1\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"NZE) NATIONAL PAYMENTS CORPORATION OF INDIA NPCIUPIOG No.186/2023-24 19\\\" December 2023 To, All Members, Unified Payments Interface (UPI) Dear Sir/Madam, Subject: Introduction of UP] TAP & PAY mode of payments In addition to the existing modes (Scan & Pay, Pay to Contact, UPI Number, etc.) of UPI Payments, “UPI Tap & Pay” is the new mode introduced for UP] transactions. Following is the construct for UPI Tap & Pay transactions:\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S2\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"serena a Oe Prt | FORWPRD NPCI/UPI/OC-186A/2026-27 10\\\" September 2026 To, Members and UPI Application Providers — Unified Payments Interface (UPI) Subject: Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS) With reference to UPI Operating Circular NPCI/UPI/OC-186/2023-24 dated 19° December 2023, UPI Tap & Pay through Near Field Communication (NFC) on QR was introduced as an additional mode for initiating UPI transactions. In addition to QR, UPI Tap & Pay shall now be extended to Point of Sale (PoS) terminals enabling Users to make contactless (NFC-based) UPI! payments by unlocking their mobile device and tapping it on the PoS terminal.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-001\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S3\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"1. UPI APPs shall ensure to provide the Tap & Pay mode of payment only through mobiles devices having NFC capability.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S4\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"Key Guidelines 1. Members and UPI Application Providers shall ensure that UPI Tap & Pay transactions on PoS terminals are accepted only for Person-to-Merchant (P2M) transactions.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Key Guidelines\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-001\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S5\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"2. UPI APPs shall take permission from the customer to enable NFC for Tap & Pay transactions.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S6\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"Payee PSP 1. Payee PSP shall enable UPI Tap & Pay only on NFC-enabled PoS terminals that are certified in accordance with the Payment Card Industry PIN Transaction Security / Contactless Payments on Commercial Off-The-Shelf (COTS) devices (PCI PTS / CPOC) standards.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Payee PSP\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"payee_psp\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-001\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S7\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"3. UPI Apps shall provide separate call to action button for Tap & Pay mode on the homepage.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S8\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 2, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"UPI Application Provider 1. UP! Application Providers / PSP Banks shall ensure explicit User consent is obtained after each device binding operation before allowing further transactions using UPI! Tap & Pay.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"UPI Application Provider\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-002\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S9\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"4. On Tap, the transaction amount of Rs.500 and less will be processed through UP! LITE account, if enabled by the user, if not, then the transaction shall be processed with UPI PIN. UPI APPs are recommended to have the App passcode, biometrics or pattern based lock in case of UPI LITE.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S10\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 2, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"Remitter Bank 1. Remitter Bank shall validate the User’s account for UPI Tap & Pay feature enablement status before processing each transaction. Further, Members & UPI Application Providers shall be consulted to provide option to Users to set their own transaction limits within the aforesaid ceiling of ₹5000. Yours sincerely, SD/- Sourabh Tomar Deputy Chief — UPI Product Page 2 of 2\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Remitter Bank\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"remitter_bank\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-002\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S11\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"5. On Tap, the transaction amount more than Rs.500 will need UP! PIN and will be processed online.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S12\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"2. Members and UPI Application Providers shall ensure explicit User consent is obtained for enabling UPI Tap & Pay feature, with Users having the ability to opt out at any time.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Key Guidelines\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-001\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S13\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"6. Members shall ensure to comply with the NPCI brand guidelines updated on NPCI website for UPI Tap & Pay.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S14\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"2. Payee PSP shall integrate the Point-of-Sale Common Library for UPI (PoS CL) at the PoS terminal and complete the integration on all the PoS terminals under its acquiring network. Page 1 of 2 1001A, The Capital, B Wing, 10\\\" Floor, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (E), Mumbai 400 O51-\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Payee PSP\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"payee_psp\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-001\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S15\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"7. UPI Tap & Pay mode of payment shall be available on mobile devices with both android/ ios operating systems.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S16\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 2, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"2. UPI Application Providers shall ensure that device lock is enabled as a prerequisite for activating UP! Tap & Pay. Further, the device shall be in an unlocked state at the time of initiating a UP! Tap & Pay transaction.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"UPI Application Provider\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-002\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S17\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"8. Initiation mode ‘06’ shall be used for UPI Tap & Pay transactions. All UP] Apps and banks shall ensure to process TAP & Pay transactions with initiation mode 06.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Document opening\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [], \"source_corrections\": null, \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S18\", \"document_id\": \"2026-OC-186A\", \"title\": \"Enhancement - UPI Tap & Pay on Point of Sale (PoS)\", \"circular_number\": \"186A\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2026-09-10\", \"text\": \"3. Members and UPI Application Providers shall ensure that per transaction limit is capped at ₹5000, up to which additional factor of authentication shall not be required.\", \"needs_priority_review\": false, \"section_heading\": \"Key Guidelines\", \"retrieval_reason\": \"document_coverage\", \"roles\": [\"upi_app\"], \"source_corrections\": [\"bootstrap-001\"], \"product_memberships\": [\"UPI\"], \"metadata_quality\": \"existing_source_metadata\", \"source_coverage\": {\"total_pages\": 2, \"empty_pages\": [], \"thin_pages\": [], \"page_count_verified\": true, \"origin\": \"existing_v04\"}}\n{\"citation\": \"S19\", \"document_id\": \"2023-UPI-186\", \"title\": \"Introduction of UPI TAP & PAY mode of Payments\", \"circular_number\": \"186\", \"page\": 1, \"issue_date\": \"2023-12-19\", \"text\": \"9. Acquiring banks shall ensure that NFC tags used inside the UPI Smart QRs/ Tags are NFC forum certified (Type 2) and non-rewritable post personalisation. Acquiring banks shall be liable for the loss occurred due to tampering, if any. Acquiring banks shall perform the periodic checks of the UPI Smart QRs installed at the merchants and ensure replacement, if requir